abstract: >-
  Figures, figure-generation code, a machine-readable taxonomy, and the full
  bibliography for a survey of explainable NLP that spans classical feature
  attribution through LLM-era mechanistic interpretability. The survey
  contributes a unified four-dimensional taxonomy of explanation methods
  (scope, mechanism, model access, output form), practical decision
  frameworks with worked examples, and a synthesis of chain-of-thought
  faithfulness, self-explanation, sparse autoencoders, and circuit tracing.
